A Dawn back end the Dawn back-end flag does not gate.

M158's patch 0035 found a WebGPU dependency use_dawn did not gate, and M161's
0045 found Blink's half of the same thing. This is that sentence once more,
one flag further in: use_dawn is TRUE in this build since M165, and what is
not gated now is not WebGPU but VULKAN.

gpu/command_buffer/service/BUILD.gn compiles three Vulkan Ozone shared-image
representations. Two of them - vulkan_ozone_image_representation and
skia_vk_ozone_image_representation - are added inside

  if (enable_vulkan) { ... if (use_ozone) { ... } }

The third is added seventy lines below inside if (use_dawn), asking only
use_ozone, and the file it names opens with

  #include <dawn/native/VulkanBackend.h>
  #include <sync/sync.h>
  #include <vulkan/vulkan.h>

so an Ozone platform with no Vulkan matches the condition as written and
cannot compile the file. sync/sync.h is libsync, which M159 removed, and the
file also reaches ui/gfx/linux/drm_util_linux.h, which is libdrm and which
patch 0037 gated - so it is on the far side of two lines this port had
already drawn, through a condition that asked about neither.

Asking enable_vulkan is the same question its two siblings already ask.

And the OTHER half, which is the mistake this whole milestone is about: the
call site. ozone_image_backing.cc includes the header and constructs the
class under BUILDFLAG(USE_DAWN) alone, so gating only the definition leaves a
caller with nothing to call - exactly what M164 found six earlier milestones
had each done once. It is graded by a link rather than by a build.

Nothing here is about this OS: any build with use_dawn = true, use_ozone =
true and enable_vulkan = false hits both halves.

diff --git a/gpu/command_buffer/service/BUILD.gn b/gpu/command_buffer/service/BUILD.gn
index 58537a332e..b8fa5687c9 100644
--- a/gpu/command_buffer/service/BUILD.gn
+++ b/gpu/command_buffer/service/BUILD.gn
@@ -513,7 +513,17 @@ target(link_target_type, "gles2_sources") {
         "shared_image/dawn_gl_texture_representation.h",
       ]
     }
-    if (use_ozone) {
+    # enable_vulkan as well as use_ozone. The file this names opens with
+    # dawn/native/VulkanBackend.h, sync/sync.h and vulkan/vulkan.h, and the
+    # condition as written asks only whether this is an Ozone platform - so an
+    # Ozone platform with no Vulkan matches it and cannot compile the file.
+    #
+    # enable_vulkan is the flag the SIBLING representation already uses:
+    # vulkan_ozone_image_representation.cc is added seventy lines above inside
+    # if (enable_vulkan) { ... if (use_ozone) }, and skia_vk_ozone with it.
+    # This is the one Vulkan Ozone representation of the three that is outside
+    # that question.
+    if (use_ozone && enable_vulkan) {
       sources += [
         "shared_image/dawn_ozone_image_representation.cc",
         "shared_image/dawn_ozone_image_representation.h",
diff --git a/gpu/command_buffer/service/shared_image/ozone_image_backing.cc b/gpu/command_buffer/service/shared_image/ozone_image_backing.cc
index 6855b869a5..97fc091637 100644
--- a/gpu/command_buffer/service/shared_image/ozone_image_backing.cc
+++ b/gpu/command_buffer/service/shared_image/ozone_image_backing.cc
@@ -55,11 +55,18 @@
 #if BUILDFLAG(USE_DAWN)
 #include "gpu/command_buffer/service/dawn_context_provider.h"
 #include "gpu/command_buffer/service/graphite_utils.h"
-#include "gpu/command_buffer/service/shared_image/dawn_ozone_image_representation.h"
 #include "gpu/command_buffer/service/shared_image/skia_graphite_dawn_image_representation.h"
 #include "third_party/skia/include/gpu/graphite/Context.h"
 #include "third_party/skia/include/gpu/graphite/Image.h"
 #include "third_party/skia/include/gpu/graphite/Recorder.h"
+
+// DawnOzoneImageRepresentation is Dawn's VULKAN representation - its own
+// first include is dawn/native/VulkanBackend.h - so it is compiled under
+// enable_vulkan, the same question vulkan_ozone_image_representation.h above
+// is compiled under. USE_DAWN alone is one condition short.
+#if BUILDFLAG(ENABLE_VULKAN)
+#include "gpu/command_buffer/service/shared_image/dawn_ozone_image_representation.h"
+#endif
 #endif  // BUILDFLAG(USE_DAWN)
 
 namespace gpu {
@@ -160,7 +167,7 @@ std::unique_ptr<DawnImageRepresentation> OzoneImageBacking::ProduceDawn(
   // Creating a representation in GPU is not allowed when usage is CPU only.
   CHECK(!(usage().Has(SHARED_IMAGE_USAGE_CPU_ONLY_READ_WRITE)));
 
-#if BUILDFLAG(USE_DAWN)
+#if BUILDFLAG(USE_DAWN) && BUILDFLAG(ENABLE_VULKAN)
   wgpu::TextureFormat webgpu_format = ToDawnFormat(format());
   if (webgpu_format == wgpu::TextureFormat::Undefined) {
     return nullptr;
@@ -169,7 +176,7 @@ std::unique_ptr<DawnImageRepresentation> OzoneImageBacking::ProduceDawn(
   return std::make_unique<DawnOzoneImageRepresentation>(
       manager, this, tracker, device, webgpu_format, std::move(view_formats),
       pixmap_);
-#else  // !BUILDFLAG(USE_DAWN)
+#else
   return nullptr;
 #endif
 }
